        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Tb(NO3)3·6H2O (0.2718 g, 0.6 mmol) was added to a methanol solution of H4L (0.3092 g, 0.4 mmol). The mixture was sonicated until complete dissolution, then aqueous NaOH (0.048 g, 1.2 mmol) was added dropwise until fully dissolved. The solution was kept in a drying oven at 338 K for 6 h, cooled to room temperature, and left for solvent evaporation for two days, giving 241 mg of transparent single crystals formulated as [Tb3(HL)2(H2O)2](NO3)3·H2O·CH3OH. Crystals were washed with acetonitrile before characterization. Ligand H4L was prepared by a published procedure.",
